# Cloudflare security headers — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# (Workers static-assets confirmed to still honor this file, same as Pages.)
#
# CSP script-src is locked down with sha256 hashes for inline scripts instead
# of 'unsafe-inline' — Astro inlines each page-specific <script> directly into
# the HTML rather than extracting it to an external file, so each one needs
# its own hash here or it's silently blocked (the script still renders, it
# just never runs). Current 11 hashes cover: BaseLayout's Person + WebSite
# JSON-LD, index.astro's WebPage + MusicAlbum JSON-LD, Faq's FAQPage JSON-LD, BaseLayout's GA4 consent-mode bootstrap + delegated data-cta
# click listener, StaffNav's scroll/menu handler, DevServices' channel-surf
# clicker, SheetMusicLibrary's search/viewer handler, Gallery's
# reel/lightbox handler (drift, ambient tilt, click-to-open — updated
# 2026-09-20 for the horizontal parallax reel), and Contact's form-submit handler (which also
# fires GA4's generate_lead event on a successful send). HeroGraded's
# terminal widget lost its rotation (and
# its <script> entirely) once the dedicated #dev section made most of its
# destinations redundant. If any of these scripts
# change, regenerate every hash with:
#   npm run build
#   node -e "const fs=require('fs'),crypto=require('crypto');
#     for (const f of ['dist/index.html','dist/404.html']) {
#       const html=fs.readFileSync(f,'utf8').replace(/<!--[\s\S]*?-->/g, '');
#       const re=/<script(?![^>]*\bsrc=)[^>]*>([\s\S]*?)<\/script>/g; let m;
#       while ((m=re.exec(html))) console.log(f,
#         'sha256-'+crypto.createHash('sha256').update(m[1],'utf8').digest('base64'));
#     }"
# and dedupe the resulting list into the script-src below. The `.replace(...)`
# strips HTML comments before scanning - found the hard way on 2026-09-20:
# BaseLayout.astro's own comment explaining the GA4 script (which literally
# contains the prose "every inline <script>") was fooling the un-stripped
# version of this regex into matching that comment's "<script>" as a fake
# opening tag and capturing everything up through the *real* GA4 script's
# closing tag as one garbled blob - producing a hash that matched nothing
# real, while the actual GA4 bootstrap script's true hash was never in this
# list at all. Console showed a CSP violation demanding a hash this exact
# process never produced; every previous "regenerate and verify" pass kept
# reporting all-clear because it re-ran the same broken regex to check its
# own output. Net effect: GA4 (and its consent-mode bootstrap, and the
# delegated data-cta click tracking) has been silently CSP-blocked on
# production since GA4 was reinstalled on 2026-09-15 - matches
# docs/todolist.md's "GA4 shows near-zero real traffic" note exactly.
#
# `npm run verify-csp` (scripts/verify-csp-hashes.mjs, wired into
# .github/workflows/e2e.yml after the build step) now diffs this file's
# hash list against a fresh build and fails CI on any mismatch - it only
# detects drift, the manual regen command above still produces the actual
# replacement hash(es).
#
# style-src still needs 'unsafe-inline' for inline style="" attributes used for
# absolute-positioned nav elements (StaffNav.astro) — same trade-off haxbyte
# made. Fonts are self-hosted (site/public/fonts/) as of 2026-09-06, so unlike
# the previous version of this file, style-src/font-src no longer need to allow
# fonts.googleapis.com/fonts.gstatic.com.
#
# static.cloudflareinsights.com (script-src) / cloudflareinsights.com
# (connect-src) are for Cloudflare Web Analytics (BaseLayout.astro's beacon
# script) — same two allowances haxbyte's CSP carries for the same reason.
# Remove both if Web Analytics is ever turned off.
#
# www.googletagmanager.com (script-src) / www.google-analytics.com +
# *.google-analytics.com (connect-src) are for GA4 (BaseLayout.astro's gtag
# snippet, reinstalled 2026-09-15, plus its delegated data-cta click
# listener that fires 'cta_click' events - added because most real CTAs
# on this page are same-origin (#contact, #dev) or mailto: links, which
# GA4 Enhanced Measurement's automatic outbound-click tracking never
# would have caught). GA4 runs in Consent Mode v2's default
# "denied" state — no consent UI on this site ever grants it — so it only
# ever sends cookieless pings, but those pings still go out to these hosts.
# Remove all three if GA4 is ever turned off.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-3vmrDsUfV0YGCh6TFpZuHplNF8I4jzLGISCmvwDah24=' 'sha256-CE0h8w6GdoQuZnMeDrHWbpg1/25kG7Hag1R+wtmv+3s=' 'sha256-GPvuy5F41har+563VvNOMgFCUaLK/gTbHgh640FWIvU=' 'sha256-MjqgbBst2Sm+GuakXD8Hqqmixd14uV2MIC2BvZ8wnZI=' 'sha256-NbShJepZBJV3NtXfnhpsV4WgESR2RjnjRweWYr0TCnc=' 'sha256-QfxzmL/sIu3tEVL4glOy+j4gP6J2YPHIYl8eNHTHlKg=' 'sha256-cInJNjbkC1iFoNU8MNT3FL1+/03g1nX4HHFBuAUAHF8=' 'sha256-l5lJdH+oL1TCt10RY+eZA7trbg9sh9CJR5Of/9SqhLI=' 'sha256-rSyqRmBtOJvY9FJN5hPhhaczRnO3TBqgcKNXpzyP+ok=' 'sha256-votDdFOvqIaIYhcVNlTD7HiBcCqk1u4WhbUl2QkV1aY=' 'sha256-ztqAppOebbaBRNdI9olAyhYcYR/cbYZfMzGRefF/mqU=' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Caching — Cloudflare Workers static-assets defaults every file to
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate` regardless of content, confirmed via `curl -I`
# against production (2026-09-06): even /_astro/*'s content-hashed bundles and
# self-hosted font files were forcing a revalidation round-trip on every load.
# /_astro/* filenames change automatically when their content does, so caching
# them forever is fully safe. /fonts/, /images/, and /sheetmusic/ aren't
# content-hashed - a shorter, non-"immutable" max-age here so a real asset
# swap (without a filename change) still reaches visitors within a week
# instead of a year.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/sheetmusic/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
